From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: a bitmap shared from another bitmap can be drawn

Microsoft 365 Word showed its ribbon's font name and font size boxes as
solid black rectangles. Word's ribbon is composited from an atlas: each
text box's content (drawn by RichEdit's TxDraw, copied into the atlas) is
drawn through a second view of the atlas that CreateSharedBitmap makes
from the atlas bitmap, with bitmap properties given (alpha ignored). Wine
gave every bitmap shared from anything but a DXGI surface the options
"target, cannot draw" whenever properties were passed, so the view had no
shader resource and drawing it drew transparent black, shown black.

A bitmap shared from another Direct2D bitmap is a second view of the same
resource; the properties passed to CreateSharedBitmap have no options, so
the view now takes the source bitmap's options, as it already did when no
properties were passed.

Test: test/d2dsharedview-gate.sh with test/d2dsharedview-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_D2D_SHARED_CANNOT_DRAW).
---
--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -483,6 +483,14 @@
         memcpy(&bitmap_desc, desc, sizeof(*desc));
         if (IsEqualIID(iid, &IID_IDXGISurface) || IsEqualIID(iid, &IID_IDXGISurface1))
             bitmap_desc.bitmapOptions = d2d_get_bitmap_options_for_surface(data);
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_D2D_SHARED_CANNOT_DRAW
+        /* Stained Glass OS: a bitmap shared from another bitmap is a second view of the same
+         * resource and can be used as that one can (the properties passed have no options);
+         * it was made a target that cannot be drawn, so drawing it drew nothing (Office draws
+         * its ribbon's text boxes from such views of its atlas: black boxes). */
+        else if (IsEqualIID(iid, &IID_ID2D1Bitmap) && data && unsafe_impl_from_ID2D1Bitmap(data))
+            bitmap_desc.bitmapOptions = unsafe_impl_from_ID2D1Bitmap(data)->options;
+#endif
         else
             bitmap_desc.bitmapOptions = D2D1_BITMAP_OPTIONS_TARGET | D2D1_BITMAP_OPTIONS_CANNOT_DRAW;
         bitmap_desc.colorContext = NULL;
